==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|mere|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪəli/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪɹli/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-merely.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[wholly|Wholly]], [[entirely]]. {{defdate|16th-20th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|year=1644| author=John Milton| title={{w|Aeropagitica}}| passage=It is not forgot, since the acute and distinct ''Arminius'' was perverted '''meerly''' by the perusing of a namelesse discourse writt'n at ''Delf'', which at first he took in hand to confute.}}
# {{lb|en|focus}} Without any other reason etc.; [[only]], [[just]], and [[nothing]] [[more]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|wholly}}<!-- either [[Thesaurus:completely]] or [[Thesaurus:solely]]; unclear which from this description -->
* {{sense|without any other reason}} See also [[Thesaurus:merely]]

